From 8fa61fa04f6081a50eb0690783ed0d35cc78a1bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Simon A. F. Lund" <os@safl.dk>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:03:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: serve DMA into another vfio-user device's BAR

A guest that points the NIC at another device's memory, such as GPU VRAM
registered with ibv_reg_dmabuf_mr(), gets a failed transfer when that device
is itself a vfio-user server: QEMU shares the peer's mmap-able BAR as a DMA
region without a file descriptor, so vfu_sgl_get() refuses it with EFAULT.
Falling back to vfu_sgl_read()/vfu_sgl_write() does not help, since on the
single socket those replies collide with the client's own requests, and QEMU
has no twin socket. --peer-memory FILE:SIZE instead names the file behind
the BAR, a peer server's memfd under /proc for example, and the server maps
it for the first fd-less region of that size, so peer-to-peer DMA works with
stock QEMU.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Simon A. F. Lund <os@safl.dk>
